      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "@id": "https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/bakersfield-ca#faqpage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What certifications do you hold?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS follows NIST SP 800-88 Rev. 2 media sanitization and DoD 5220.22-M destruction practices for retired drives and tapes collected in Bakersfield. We also support HIPAA 45 CFR 164.312 workflows, including Business Associate Agreements when a healthcare engagement requires them. Kern County hospitals and clinics receive serial-level certificates after processing. Documentation is packaged for audit files, typically within 48 hours after processing completes. Pickup is scheduled for qualifying commercial volumes across Bakersfield and nearby plants."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What areas do you serve?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We provide free scheduled pickup across Bakersfield and the greater Kern County area, including Rosedale, Oildale, Downtown, and East Bakersfield. Regional stops can be arranged for qualifying volumes at nearby agricultural plants and energy offices in Wasco, Shafter, Delano, Arvin, Taft, and Lamont. Tehachapi, McFarland, Ridgecrest, and California City can be included on regional runs. Organizations searching for electronics recycling near me throughout Bakersfield find STS provides free pickup in Rosedale, Oildale, and all Kern County locations."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is pickup really free?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Commercial pickup is free for qualifying volumes of computers and electronics across Bakersfield and Kern County. We typically confirm eligibility on the intake call so your team sees no surprise haul fees. Working devices may qualify for remarketing credits that offset disposal costs, with no hidden haul fees on approved pickups. Complimentary pickup is available for qualifying volumes across Bakersfield and nearby plants, including energy offices and food-processing sites."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you provide audit documentation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Every Bakersfield engagement includes chain of custody records, asset tags, downstream weights, and a Certificate of Destruction. Accurate reporting is then packaged for your compliance file, typically within 48 hours after processing completes. Serial numbers appear on the certificate when devices are tagged. Kern County healthcare, government, and education organizations use these records for HIPAA, surplus, and internal security reviews."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can you handle large-scale ITAD projects?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Our 200,000 sq ft processing operation handles campus refreshes, warehouse scanner fleets, and full data center takeouts for Bakersfield organizations. Education fleets on the scale of Kern High School District are planned as staged, serialized multi-day pickups. California State University, Bakersfield labs and County of Kern departments can be coordinated as multi-building jobs. Same-week scheduling is typical after a short inventory of retired devices."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does pickup take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Pickup for most Bakersfield organizations is typically scheduled the same week after a brief phone inventory of devices. Larger multi-building ITAD projects use coordinated weekend windows that limit downtime for operations and facilities staff. Share a device list or photos so we can confirm free pickup eligibility for qualifying Bakersfield volumes. Our secure fleet serves Bakersfield with scheduled pickups near CA-99 and throughout the Downtown area."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What electronics can be recycled in Bakersfield?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Desktop PCs, laptops, servers, networking gear, printers, copiers, monitors, phones, and legacy electronics from Bakersfield offices and plants. We also process ink and toner, old electronics, and data center equipment. Packing plants at firms such as Grimmway Farms retire scanners, PCs, and warehouse handhelds. California treats covered electronics as universal waste under DTSC and CalRecycle rules, so landfill disposal is not allowed for these devices."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much does electronics recycling cost?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "When Bakersfield organizations need secure IT disposal, STS offers free pickup for qualifying volumes. Working devices may qualify for remarketing credits that offset costs, with no hidden haul fees on approved pickups. Volume discounts are available for campus refreshes and plant collections across Kern County. Eligibility is typically confirmed on the intake call before a Bakersfield pickup is scheduled."
          }
        }
